From 5a66579a3d307dddb2f8d917392cdaa8af9a0127 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Parada <fparada@meatcode.cl>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:57:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] MUSEUM FIX (2026-08-10): guard
 emscripten_set_running_machine to non-libretro builds

running_machine::start() calls emscripten_set_running_machine(this) under
#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) (line ~317), but the definition is guarded by
#if defined(EMSCRIPTEN) && !defined(__LIBRETRO__) (line ~1298).

In the libretro build the call compiled but the definition did not, so the
link failed with:

  Aborted(missing function:
  _ZN15running_machine30emscripten_set_running_machineEPS_)

Fixed by adding && !defined(__LIBRETRO__) to the call-site guard so the
call is excluded in libretro builds. The libretro core uses its own
retro_main_loop, not the Emscripten loop.

MUST be re-applied on any future mame0.243 rebuild -- this is a source
edit, not a build flag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/emu/machine.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/emu/machine.cpp b/src/emu/machine.cpp
index 77ef8afc2e..c1296b0cbe 100644
--- a/src/emu/machine.cpp
+++ b/src/emu/machine.cpp
@@ -314,7 +314,7 @@ int running_machine::run(bool quiet)
 
 		export_http_api();
 
-#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) && !defined(__LIBRETRO__)
 		// break out to our async javascript loop and halt
 		emscripten_set_running_machine(this);
 #endif
